  &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191177/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/niw2deybmislnoi07vqf.jpg" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191177/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;The &lt;em&gt;State of Devs&lt;/em&gt; 2026 survey results are out&lt;/a&gt; with over 5,000 developers sharing their thoughts on software development career security, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191178/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;AI use/sentiment&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191179/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;hobbies&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191180/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;the workplace&lt;/a&gt; (including income).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191181/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Why does &lt;code&gt;example.com&lt;/code&gt; now load JavaScript?&lt;/a&gt; The IANA says since most clients hitting the site are automated and don't load JavaScript, it's a way to save bandwidth. There's &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191182/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;more on the site's recent redesign here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify explains &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191183/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;how it reduced Edge Function invocation latency by ~5x&lt;/a&gt;, switching from hosted V8 isolates to Unikraft MicroVMs on its own edge network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤖 &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191184/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Pi 1.0&lt;/a&gt;, the minimal Node.js-based coding agent, adds MCP and non-LLM model support through 'Codemode'. They also launched an experimental &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191185/rss" style=" color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;   "&gt;Pi Durable&lt;/a&gt; runtime for running resilient, long-term agent flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
